  "behavior": {
    "ownership": "QuerySession acquires an owned core lease for the checked source path and descriptor. The project registry holds only Weak references; a numeric RPC sourceRestriction ID describes the owner and cannot recreate the Arc capability.",
    "limits": "At most 16 live core source owners per project session. Dead weak entries are inert immediately and collected on the next acquisition. IDs advance with checked arithmetic and are never reused within that registry.",
    "competingWrites": "The common can_edit boundary blocks scalar and dependent property files, including exact history replay. Legacy direct query planning rejects a protected owner; the owning QuerySession supplies its unforgeable lease to the same source/support check.",
    "rename": "Preview and apply inspect text changes and both sides of directory moves. Existing rename Undo/Redo receives the same registry; unrelated structural refresh retains restrictions. Opaque project-journal recovery rejects active owners before attempting writes.",
    "lifetime": "Close drops only the source session lease. Checkpoint removal drops its linked handle. Proposed transactional clones retain the same lease until they are committed or dropped. EOF or metadata session destruction cannot leave a live global filesystem lock.",
    "policy": "No source permissions, native override, or persistent IDE setting is changed. Releasing a source session does not release a support-policy or user restriction.",
    "scope": "Restrictions affect operations in the owning ProjectSession/backend. A different process or IDE may change disk; exact source/descriptor/context guards detect those changes before source application. There is no global filesystem freeze.",
    "rpc": "API 1.15/1.16 SessionHeader adds optional protection.sourceRestriction. Native ownerLock remains null and bslEditing remains false. Rename issue source_session_active is localized by the adapter in ru/en.",
    "headlessBsl": "Core tests use explicit synthetic native lock acknowledgement 19. This proves backend ownership and source checks only; it is not acceptance of a native BSL editor freeze.",
    "protectedViews": "The general protected-view provider is not migrated in this part. Query owner snapshots and recovery already come from ESKA; the ordinary support provider still reads file bytes through the IDE.",
    "newDependencies": false,
    "backendWritesQueryOwner": false
  },
